OL,3,GNEWSAFamily of charity's founder marks
OL,4,A150th birthday
OL,5,
OL,6,F"It is a bit of an honour, really, to
OL,7,Fknow that you've got somebody of that
OL,8,Fcalibre in your family tree," said
OL,9,FRichard Jebb.
OL,11,FHe is the great-great-nephew of
OL,12,FEglantyne Jebb, born in Ellesmere,
OL,13,FShropshire, who set up the Save the
OL,14,FChildren charity with her sister
OL,15,FDorothy in 1919.
OL,17,FSpecial celebrations are taking place
OL,18,Fto mark Eglantyne's 150th birthday,
OL,19,Fincluding remembrance services and the
OL,20,Funveiling of a new artwork.
OL,23,APub: 25-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
